{{Quote|This R5 astromech is built for adventure.''"<br />[R5-D4 objects]<br />"''What&mdash; of course you are! You're supposed to be piloting starfighters across the galaxy and fighting tyranny!|[[Peli Motto]], on R5-D4, even as the droid was falling apart|<ref name="Chapter 18">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref>}}
The '''R5 series astromech droid''',<ref name="Rebel Fighters Manual">''[[Rebel Starfighters Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref> also known as the '''R5 line'''<ref name="SWCT">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=R5-D4 - Astromech Droid}}</ref> was a model of [[R-series]] [[astromech droid]]<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]].<ref name="BB-8 and others" />

==History==
{{Quote|Oh, come on, now. Don't be a coward. You're an astromech. Act like one!|Peli Motto, to R5-D4|<ref name="Chapter 18" />}}
Cut-price versions of superior [[R2-series astromech droid|R2 units]],<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> they were low cost, but prone to malfunctions,<ref name="Card Trader">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=R5-D4 - Astromech Droid}}</ref> defects, and bad attitudes.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Standing 0.97 [[meter]]s in height,<ref name="R5-D4" /> they generally had shorter, cone-shaped heads<ref name="Droids">''[[Star Wars Builders: Droids]]''</ref> and were equipped with repair [[Limb|arms]].<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Their reputation was so bad that their manufacturer, Industrial Automaton, had to pull the model from the market to save their own reputation.<ref name="BB-8 and others" /> [[LX-R5]] served [[Jedi Master]] [[Kelleran Beq]].<ref name="Episode 1">{{JTC|1}}</ref> [[R5-D4]] was one of the last units produced in the R5 line.<ref name="Card Trader" />

R5-D4,<ref name="Chapter 18" /> [[R5-D8]], [[R5-K6]],<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> and [[Essfour|S4]] were R5 droids that served the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Star Wars 26">[[Star Wars (2015) 26|''Star Wars'' (2015) 26]]</ref>

